interface ABANDSResult { upper: HaasNumberCollection; middle: HaasNumberCollection; lower: HaasNumberCollection; 1: HaasNumberCollection; 2: HaasNumberCollection; 3: HaasNumberCollection; [index: number]: HaasNumberCollection }

-- Acceleration Bands (ABANDS) created by Price Headley.
-- Plots bands around a simple moving average as the midpoint and the upper and lower
-- bands are of equal distance from this midpoint.
-- Look for breakouts outside these bands, while also using the shorter time frames
-- to define likely support and resistance levels at the lower and upper Acceleration Bands. This indicator is usually plotted on the price chart.
declare function ABANDS(high: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, low: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, close: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, period: number | HaasNumberCollection): ABANDSResult

-- Accumulation/Distribution Line (AD) Developed by Marc Chaikin, the Accumulation Distribution
-- Line is a volume-based indicator designed to measure the cumulative flow of money into and out of a security. Chaikin
-- originally referred to the indicator as the Cumulative Money Flow Line. As with cumulative indicators, the Accumulation
-- Distribution Line is a running total of each period's Money Flow Volume. First, a multiplier is calculated based on the
-- relationship of the close to the high-low range. Second, the Money Flow Multiplier is multiplied by the period's volume
-- to come up with a Money Flow Volume. A running total of the Money Flow Volume forms the Accumulation Distribution Line. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function AD(high: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, low: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, close: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, volume: number[] | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Developed by Marc Chaikin, the Chaikin Oscillator (ADOSC) measures the momentum of the
-- Accumulation Distribution Line using the MACD formula. (This makes it an indicator of an indicator.)
-- The Chaikin Oscillator is the difference between the 3-day and 10-day EMAs of the Accumulation Distribution
-- Line. Like other momentum indicators, this indicator is designed to anticipate directional changes in the
-- Accumulation Distribution Line by measuring the momentum behind the movements.
-- A momentum change is the first step to a trend change. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function ADOSC(high: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, low: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, close: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, volume: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, fastPeriod: number | HaasNumberCollection, slowPeriod: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- The Average Directional Index (ADX) depicts a presence or absence of a trend.
-- ADX advices on the strength of the dominant forces that move market prices here and now.
-- In other words, ADX advices on trend tendencies: whether the trend is going to continue
-- and strengthen or it is about to lose its positions. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function ADX(high: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, low: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, close: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, period: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Average Directional Movement Index Rating (ADXR) is a smoothed version
-- of ADX indicator and is used as a rating of the Directional Movement while smoothing out ADX values.
-- If to compare ADXR to ADX, the smoother ADXR doesn't depend much on fast short-term market turns and
-- reversals, which allows to minimize trading risks when relying on ADXR in the long term. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function ADXR(high: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, low: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, close: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, period: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- The Awesome Oscillator (AO) shows the difference in between the 5 SMA and 34 SMA.
-- If to be precise, 5 SMA of mid-prices is subtracted from 34 SMA of mid-prices which allows to see the market momentum. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function AO(hl2prices: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, shortLength: number | HaasNumberCollection, longLength: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- The Absolute Price Oscillator (APO) displays the difference between two
-- exponential moving averages of an asset's price and is expressed as an absolute value. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function APO(prices: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, fastPeriod: number | HaasNumberCollection, slowPeriod: number | HaasNumberCollection, maType?: EnumMovingAverages): HaasNumberCollection

interface AROONResult { aroonDn: HaasNumberCollection; aroonUp: HaasNumberCollection; 1: HaasNumberCollection; 2: HaasNumberCollection; [index: number]: HaasNumberCollection }

-- Aroon indicator is a young one, developed by Tushar Chande in 1995.
-- Aroon was created to measure the strength of a trend and potentials for its continuation as well
-- as the quality and type of the trend: up-trend, down-trend or sideways moving market. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function AROON(high: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, low: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, period: number | HaasNumberCollection): AROONResult

-- Aroon oscillator is based on Aroon Indicator. Aroon Oscillator is
-- a trend-following indicator that illustrates the strength of a current trend and its potentials to last. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function AROONOSC(high: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, low: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, period: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- The Average True Range (ATR), developed by Wilder, gives traders a feel of what the historical volatility
-- was in order to prepare for trading in the actual market.
-- Currency pairs that get lower ATR readings suggest lower market volatility, while currency pairs with higher
-- ATR indicator readings require appropriate trading adjustments according to higher volatility.
-- Wilder used the Moving average to smooth out the ATR indicator readings, so that ATR looks the way we know it. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function ATR(high: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, low: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, close: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, period: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- The Average Deviation (AVGDEV) is simply an averaged version of the Standard Deviation (STDDEV). This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function AVGDEV(close: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, period: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- The Average Price (AVGPRICE) is the price between open, high, low and close (aka OHLC/4). This indicator is usually plotted on the price chart.
declare function AVGPRICE(open: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, high: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, low: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, close: number[] | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Calculates an absolute/positive number.
declare function Abs(input: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Compares the average entry price to current price, absolute value-based.
declare function AbsolutePriceChange(amount?: number | HaasNumberCollection, targetPrice?: number | HaasNumberCollection, positionId?: string): boolean

-- Gets the main account guid of the bot.
declare function AccountGuid(): string

-- Calculates the angle whose cosine is the specified number.
declare function Acos(input: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Adds numbers/tables and returns the result number/table.
declare function Add(input1: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection, input2?: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Add a percentage to the value.
declare function AddPerc(value: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection, percentage: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Add a percentage to the value.
declare function AddPercentage(value: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection, percentage: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Adjusts an Unix timestamp.
declare function AdjustTimestamp(unix?: number | HaasNumberCollection, addSeconds?: number | HaasNumberCollection, addMinutes?: number | HaasNumberCollection, addHours?: number | HaasNumberCollection, addMonths?: number | HaasNumberCollection, addDays?: number | HaasNumberCollection, addYears?: number | HaasNumberCollection): number

-- Adjusts a virtual bot position by processing a simulated order using the defined specifications. Works similarly to PlaceExitLongOrder/PlaceExitShortOrder, but will NOT create a real order; it is only simulated.
declare function AdjustVPosition(price: number | HaasNumberCollection, amount: number | HaasNumberCollection, positionId?: string): nil

-- Gets the amount label. For reflection, in case the market is Bitstamp BTC/USDit will return 'BTC'. When we are on BitMEX XBT/USD (XBTUSD), it will return 'contract(s)'.
declare function AmountCurrency(market?: string): string

-- Returns a number of how many decimals is allowed for order amounts.
declare function AmountDecimals(market?: string, amount?: number | HaasNumberCollection): number

-- Gets the amount label. For reflection, in case the market is Bitstamp BTC/USDit will return 'BTC'. When we are on BitMEX XBT/USD (XBTUSD), it will return 'contract(s)'.
declare function AmountLabel(market?: string): string

-- Returns the minimum allowed trade amount step for market.
declare function AmountStep(market?: string): number

-- Validates all values on being true.
declare function And(...: boolean): boolean

-- Returns true if the array contains any element or an element matches a specific value.
declare function ArrayAny(input: any, value?: any | nil): boolean

-- Returns true if the array contains any element or an element matches a specific value.
declare function ArrayContains(input: any, value?: any | nil): boolean

-- Returns a new list of the positions of the matching values. Matching rules are set by filterType. The positions depend on the input type. On a Lua table they are 1-based, so they can be used directly as an index (t[i]). On a series (a price source or HNC) they are 0-based: the newest bar is position 0, so add 1 before using one as an index (close[i + 1]). Using a series result directly as an index reads the next newer bar (one bar closer to the newest), and a match on the newest bar (0) stops the script with an out-of-range error.
declare function ArrayFind(input: any, value: any, filterType?: EnumArrayFilterTypes): any

-- Gets the value on a specific index. A negative index will take from the end of the array.
declare function ArrayGet(input: any, index: number | HaasNumberCollection): any

-- Gets the value on a specific index. A negative index will take from the end of the array.
declare function ArrayIndex(input: any, index: number | HaasNumberCollection): any

-- Gets the last value of the array with an optional offset.
declare function ArrayLast(input: any, offset?: number | HaasNumberCollection): any

-- Computes the sum of the array. Can be used in combination with a list of numbers or container results like GetAllOpenOrders() or GetAllFilledOrders().
declare function ArraySum(input: any, key?: string): number

-- Calculates the angle whose sine is the specified number.
declare function Asin(input: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Gets the buy/ask prices.
declare function AskPrices(interval?: number | HaasNumberCollection, fullCandles?: boolean, market?: string, hlcStyle?: boolean): HaasNumberCollection

-- Calculates the angle whose tangent is the specified number.
declare function Atan(input: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Calculates the angle whose tangent is the quotient of two specified numbers.
declare function Atan2(input1: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection, input2: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Calculates the average value of the array, two numbers or averages between 2 arrays.
declare function Average(input1: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection, input2?: number | number[] | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Calculates the average value of the array for a certain period.
declare function Average2(input: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, period?: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- Calculates the average candle body size of the last 50 minutes.
declare function AverageCandleSize(market?: string): number

-- Gets the average enter price.
declare function AverageEnterPrice(positionId?: string): number

-- Gets the average exit price.
declare function AverageExitPrice(positionId?: string): number

-- Calculates the average orderbook bid/ask spread of the last 50 minutes.
declare function AverageOrderbookSpread(market?: string): number

interface BBANDSResult { upper: HaasNumberCollection; middle: HaasNumberCollection; lower: HaasNumberCollection; 1: HaasNumberCollection; 2: HaasNumberCollection; 3: HaasNumberCollection; [index: number]: HaasNumberCollection }

-- The Bollinger Band (BBANDS) study created
-- by John Bollinger plots upper and lower envelope bands around the
-- price of the instrument. The width of the bands is based on the
-- standard deviation of the closing prices from a moving average of
-- price. This indicator is usually plotted on the price chart.
declare function BBANDS(prices: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, period: number | HaasNumberCollection, devUp: number | HaasNumberCollection, devDn: number | HaasNumberCollection, maType?: EnumMovingAverages): BBANDSResult

-- The Beta (BETA) value can measure he volatility of a coin in relation to that of the market.
-- For stock investors the beta value[1] of a portfolio is an important measure of risk, a value above 1 means the
-- investment is more volatile than the market, a value lower than 1 is less volatile.
-- It can be helpful to do a beta analysis for your portfolio to see how returns match up against the beta and
-- spot real winners (low beta, high returns). Since most altcoins are still sold and bought using Bitcoin (BTC),
-- its price could be used as the [Market's source data] (2nd input parameter), which results BTC a beta of 1. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function BETA(prices1: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, prices2: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, period: number | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

-- The Balance of Power (BOP) indicator measures the market
-- strength of buyers against sellers by assessing the ability of each side to drive prices to an extreme level.
-- The resulting values can be smoothed by a moving average. This indicator is usually plotted to its own chart.
declare function BOP(open: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, high: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, low: number[] | HaasNumberCollection, close: number[] | HaasNumberCollection): HaasNumberCollection

interface BalanceResult { available: number; locked: number; total: number; 1: number; 2: number; 3: number; [index: number]: number }

-- Available, locked and total balance of a currency.
declare function Balance(accountId?: string, coin?: string, market?: string): BalanceResult

-- Total balance value of a specific currency. Including order and position margin. Does not work yet in backtests and for simulated accounts.
declare function BalanceAmount(accountId?: string, coin?: string, market?: string): number

-- Returns the base currency of the market. For reflection, in case we are on Bitstamp BTC/USD it will return 'BTC'.
declare function BaseCurrency(market?: string): string

-- A collection with sell/ask prices. Sorted from new to old.
declare function BidPrices(interval?: number | HaasNumberCollection, fullCandles?: boolean, market?: string, hlcStyle?: boolean): HaasNumberCollection

-- Converts 4 boolean values to a signal.
declare function BoolToSignal(isLong?: boolean, isShort?: boolean, isExit?: boolean, isNone?: boolean): EnumSignal

-- Send a text message to Discord.
declare function BroadcastToDiscord(message: string): nil

-- Send a text message to your Telegram.
